import torch
from torch import nn
from torch.nn import functional as F

DEVICE = torch.device("cuda" if torch.cuda.is_available() else "cpu")  # A T4 on Kaggle; CPU works for FAST runs.
N_FOLDS = 5
EPOCHS = 2 if FAST else 25  # Fixed for every fold; no early stopping, so both schemes train identically.
LR = 1e-3

%% md
The model is the repository's temporal CNN: coordinates and velocity in, six depthwise-separable convolution blocks over time, about 330k parameters. It trains in seconds per epoch on a T4, which is what makes ten runs affordable. The model and training code is shared with the rest of the series and collapsed here.

